WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.100
On top of the Yonko and the admirals, the one&nbsp;
piece manga just revealed a whole new group of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:10.140
incredibly powerful fighters called the Holy&nbsp;
Knights, that might end up becoming the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:15.420
powerful group of fighters in the entire story&nbsp;
and the final enemies of the straw hats in their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:19.740
battle against Imu. And you won’t believe all&nbsp;
of the crazy secrets about the identities of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.740 --> 00:00:24.120
these mysterious fighters that are being set&nbsp;
loose to destroy the world. Plus we finally&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:28.740
learned what happened during the Reverie and we&nbsp;
also see the true powers of the revolutionary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.740 --> 00:00:33.360
army revealed in a battle so destructive&nbsp;
it could have destroyed an entire island.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:38.280
But of course we have to start with the holy&nbsp;
knights. Now, this group was actually first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:43.440
name dropped in chapter 1054, when Akainu&nbsp;
revealed that holy knights are responsible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:49.800
for resolving disputes in the holy land. But&nbsp;
does that mean they just work for the celestial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:54.720
dragons? Or can they even hand out justice&nbsp;
to the world nobles themselves? Either way,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.720 --> 00:01:00.000
they must be pretty damn important – not to&nbsp;
mention super powerful – to become the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:04.140
governments ultimate warriors. And&nbsp;
if you’re wondering if they are even&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.140 --> 00:01:08.280
stronger than the admirals, stick around,&nbsp;
because we’ll discuss that in just a moment.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:02:34.500
But first in this chapter we get this panel of&nbsp;
the Holy Knights as Dragon says that with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:40.620
Holy Knights making their move, the real battle&nbsp;
starts for the Revolutionary army. We learn that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:46.080
these nine knights they are being sent out to&nbsp;
literally destroy kingdoms that are rebelling from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:51.780
the World Government. These kingdoms decided to&nbsp;
break off when they found out about what happened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.780 --> 00:03:00.900
to this kingdom that got destroyed by the insane&nbsp;
light attack [ch 1060]. But the fact that these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:06.540
kingdoms even know this information makes me&nbsp;
wonder how they learned about the kingdom’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:12.600
destruction? Did Sabo leak the information?&nbsp;
Or did the world find out some other way?

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:18.000
Anyway, back to the Holy Knights. These nine&nbsp;
insane fighters are tasked with dealing with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:24.120
these rebel kingdoms, and we have to assume the&nbsp;
worst here. These kingdoms are probably going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.120 --> 00:03:30.300
be wiped out entirely, or at least the rulers will&nbsp;
be killed and replaced. And this gives us some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:35.880
hint of how strong these knights really are. Since&nbsp;
there are nine knights and eight rebel kingdoms,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:41.580
I’m wondering if each knight will take out one of&nbsp;
the kingdoms or if they will work as a group and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:49.320
go one by one. Personally, if these knights are&nbsp;
so powerful I’m pretty sure that they can take out&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:54.600
a normal kingdom on their own. I mean, Sanji’s&nbsp;
brothers basically took out an entire kingdom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.600 --> 00:04:00.240
with just the help of some clones [ch 828], so&nbsp;
I’d think the Holy Knights have to be at least&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:05.160
that strong. And since Sanji’s brothers were able&nbsp;
to take out some of Big Mom’s strongest children,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:09.353
that puts these Knights at least on the level of&nbsp;
a Yonko Commander. *Emphasize with some motion*&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.353 --> 00:04:13.680
Again, AT LEAST. And if they are going&nbsp;
to match up with the straw hats later on,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.680 --> 00:04:19.680
better be at least this strong or they won’t stand&nbsp;
a chance. Because it would be truly disappointing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.680 --> 00:04:27.000
if Oda introduced 9 unknown powerful characters&nbsp;
this late in the story that then end up like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:31.440
Kaido’s Tobi Roppo, who, in the end, didn’t&nbsp;
make that much of an impact in the story.

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:40.140
However, could they be EVEN Stronger? since Dragon&nbsp;
seems to see these 9 as the ultimate force of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.140 --> 00:04:46.500
world government, there is a pretty good chance&nbsp;
they might be even stronger than the admirals.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:52.200
Which might make sense, given that many of the&nbsp;
strongest Marines, including even Akainu himself,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.200 --> 00:04:58.200
don’t like doing the dirty work of the world&nbsp;
nobles. So if many of the marines flipped sides&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:04.080
to join Luffy during the final battle, having&nbsp;
not only the seraphim, but a whole new group of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:09.780
god-like warriors that fights for Imu and the&nbsp;
world nobles would make a whole lot of sense.

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:14.280
But now let’s put on our tinfoil&nbsp;
hats. Because from the images we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:18.240
got in this chapter, plus other&nbsp;
clues we can pull from the story,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:25.560
I think we paint a pretty decent picture of&nbsp;
who these insanely strong knights could be.

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:30.720
Starting obviously with this one right here [show&nbsp;
image of Knight that looks like Shanks], who could&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:37.560
very well be Shanks’ long lost brother or&nbsp;
father. Just the picture alone shows many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:43.140
striking similarities. Such as a similar body&nbsp;
type, clothes, and even a similar sword. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.140 --> 00:05:48.480
unless these knights are shape shifters,&nbsp;
then this guy is probably related to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.480 --> 00:05:52.320
Red Haired Emperor. And before you go crazy&nbsp;
in the comments, just remember that Shanks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:56.760
is actually from the Figarland family which, as&nbsp;
we explain in my complete story of Shanks video,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.760 --> 00:06:02.160
means that he was most likely a celestial&nbsp;
dragon that got separated from his family. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.160 --> 00:06:08.640
what if the Figarland family had another son,&nbsp;
maybe even a twin, who became one of the Holy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.640 --> 00:06:15.060
Knights. Or another super interesting idea is&nbsp;
what if the Knights are all from the Figarland&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:20.040
family. Kinda like a single overpowered&nbsp;
family who protect the Celestial Dragons.

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:26.340
But wait, there's even more mind-blowing evidence&nbsp;
for this idea, and it comes from chapter 907,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:34.260
and the famous scene of Shanks meeting with the&nbsp;
Five Elders. So here me out, what if this wasn’t&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:40.380
actually Shanks, but instead it was his&nbsp;
identical brother. And damn this would go&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.380 --> 00:06:45.240
a long way towards explaining one of the&nbsp;
most controversial and mysterious scenes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:51.000
in the entire story. DO I EVEN NEED TO TELL&nbsp;
YOU how many crazy videos were spawned from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:56.940
this one scene? Shanks is Evil! The history of&nbsp;
Evil Shanks! Shanks is using Luffy! Honestly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:56.940 --> 00:07:01.500
this scene broke the fanbase and we have&nbsp;
yet to get a real explanation for it. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:08.280
never knew how Shanks got in or why the Gorosei&nbsp;
would agree to meet him, but now it is possible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:13.440
Oda was just toying with us all this time,&nbsp;
because it wasn’t even Shanks but his brother.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:21.000
I mean, we never actually hear the&nbsp;
Elders call this person by name.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:25.740
And we never see the scar or missing&nbsp;
arm. And if this was a Holy Knight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:29.340
it would make sense that the Gorosei&nbsp;
would agree to meet with them.

00:07:29.340 --> 00:07:34.020
But that’s not even the end of the evidence&nbsp;
because in an interview with Japanese TV that my&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:39.540
friend artur from the library of ohara translated&nbsp;
on his website, the author of One Piece was asked&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:47.220
if Shanks is actually two different people. This&nbsp;
was asked with the context that Shanks seems to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:51.960
be able to move quickly around the world, like&nbsp;
when he stopped Kaido from coming to Marineford&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:57.660
and then shortly after showed up at the war with&nbsp;
his crew. And it seems like Oda-sensei actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:57.660 --> 00:08:04.020
answered the question but it was censored from&nbsp;
the show. So that could mean that this theory is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:11.580
entirely possible. I mean, if it wasn’t true,&nbsp;
wouldn’t he just have come out and said that?

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:16.980
But with all the incredible speculation about&nbsp;
this Shanks-looking Knight, what about the others?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:26.100
Well, we can see that one of them wears some sort&nbsp;
of hat, and this one here has horns. So what if&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:31.380
Holy Knights are actually somehow related to the&nbsp;
other Yonko, such as Kaido and Big Mom. I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:37.020
Kaido certainly has horns. And Big Mom used to&nbsp;
wear a similar looking hat [ch 1041 or other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:37.020 --> 00:08:40.620
image of younger big mom]. However, they can’t&nbsp;
all be related like Shanks and his possible twin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:47.100
but now I’m wondering if they are clones of strong&nbsp;
pirates. I mean, with everything going on at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:51.780
Egghead Island, cloning is certainly a possibility&nbsp;
as cloning was even a thing 20 years ago.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:55.860
But at this point, we’ve thrown out&nbsp;
three Emperor’s as possible members&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:55.860 --> 00:09:00.180
of these Holy Knights. But now let’s&nbsp;
raise the stakes even higher. What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:00.180 --> 00:09:04.080
would you say if I told you that some of&nbsp;
the most legendary figures from the past,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:04.080 --> 00:09:09.720
such as Joy Boy himself, were a part of the Holy&nbsp;
Knights. Don’t believe me. Well, keep watching.

00:09:09.720 --> 00:09:17.100
So in chapter 906, we first meet this mysterious&nbsp;
cloaked figure, Imu, who we later learn is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:22.860
secret ruler of the world. And after they climb&nbsp;
this ridiculously large staircase, they arrive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.860 --> 00:09:29.040
at some secret chamber that is ice cold. Here we&nbsp;
see the famous image of this frozen straw hat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:34.140
which has led to an even greater host of&nbsp;
theories about Joy Boy and this mysterious king.

00:09:34.140 --> 00:09:39.300
BUT one possibility that I want to throw out&nbsp;
there is that this freezer is actually where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:45.540
the Holy Knights live AND that some of them are&nbsp;
the preserved fighters from the ancient past. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:49.920
there’s a few pieces of evidence to support&nbsp;
this, such as the zombie fighters from&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:49.920 --> 00:09:54.960
Thriller Bark being frozen to preserve their&nbsp;
bodies. Plus Imu is ascending these massive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:54.960 --> 00:10:01.020
stairs, almost like they are ascending into heaven&nbsp;
to reach the Holy Knights. But the most compelling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.020 --> 00:10:04.200
evidence is this image right here [show image&nbsp;
linked in the research section]. Directly above&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:10.260
the frozen straw hat, is this image of a cross&nbsp;
looking symbol. Now what is this symbol, we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:10.260 --> 00:10:16.260
don’t know exactly, but it is very similar to the&nbsp;
World Government’s cross AND a famous symbol of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:16.260 --> 00:10:21.480
the Knights Templar [show red Templar cross] which&nbsp;
we will discuss more about in just a few minutes.

00:10:21.480 --> 00:10:25.380
But if this is the symbol that represents the&nbsp;
Holy Knights, then that would mean that each&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.380 --> 00:10:30.240
of these little alcoves in this freezer could&nbsp;
be the resting place of one of the knights.

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:35.220
Alright, but that was a lot of wild speculation&nbsp;
from just this small detail – but man it’s just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.220 --> 00:10:39.180
so much fun and part of the reason&nbsp;
we read one piece in the first place.

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:45.780
But we’re not quite done with the Holy knights&nbsp;
yet, because there are even more connections to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.780 --> 00:10:52.080
famous characters in the story. For example,&nbsp;
Mihawk could be a former Holy knight. I mean,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:59.520
he’s always had a heavy Christian religious theme&nbsp;
and the markings on his famous giant sword are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:59.520 --> 00:11:05.640
very similar to the markings on Imu’s empty&nbsp;
throne. He has the same ring shaped eyes and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:12.000
we have no idea what his origin story is or how&nbsp;
he became THE strongest swordsman in One Piece.

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:17.760
The former warlord Barthelomew Kuma is another&nbsp;
character with ties to Christian religion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:22.560
since he used to carry around his giant&nbsp;
bible. So was he a holy knight in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.560 --> 00:11:27.420
past two? Did he go around smacking the&nbsp;
gospel into enemies of the world government?

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:31.800
There is also the idea that the Holy&nbsp;
Knights could be descendants of Lunarians,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:35.760
the race that used to live on top of&nbsp;
the grand line and were called gods,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:38.760
but there’s not much evidence&nbsp;
to support that right now.

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:48.300
But moving on, it's time to throw on your&nbsp;
history hat on top of your theory hat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:53.040
because we’re going to do a short de-tour&nbsp;
down everyone’s favorite rabbit hole,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:58.080
religious symbolism in one piece. And that’s&nbsp;
because the first thing I thought of when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:07.380
I heard about these Holy Knights, were the&nbsp;
legendary Knights Templar. This is a famous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:07.380 --> 00:12:14.160
group of religious warriors who fought for&nbsp;
Christianity in medieval Europe. And there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:14.160 --> 00:12:18.960
are a few truly interesting connections&nbsp;
between the Templars and the Holy Knights.

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:23.400
First, the Templars were supposedly&nbsp;
founded by nine original members,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:28.200
which included warriors as well as monks.&nbsp;
Which makes me wonder if we could see some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:28.200 --> 00:12:31.620
non-fighters with the Holy Knights as&nbsp;
well. On top of that, in the bible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:31.620 --> 00:12:37.680
the number 9&nbsp;symbolizes divine completeness or&nbsp;
conveys the meaning of finality. There are also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:37.680 --> 00:12:41.340
the obvious similarities between the Templars'&nbsp;
red cross symbol and the World Government’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:41.340 --> 00:12:45.360
cross. So basically what I’m reading into all&nbsp;
of this is that the World Government is really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:51.480
some massive cult that took over the world. Oh&nbsp;
no, Luffy please save us all. On top of that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:51.480 --> 00:12:56.580
the Templar’s duty was to protect travelers&nbsp;
visiting the holy land, but that is a little&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:56.580 --> 00:13:01.680
bit twisted in the story because now these Holy&nbsp;
Knights are protecting these so-called “gods”.

00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:07.080
But the Templars aren’t the only major symbol&nbsp;
related to these nine Holy Knights. And we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:07.080 --> 00:13:11.580
might be able to figure out some more about&nbsp;
these Knights just based on the number nine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.580 --> 00:13:16.620
itself. First, there are nine Rio Poneglyphs which&nbsp;
supposedly tell the true history of the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:20.280
so could these knights be someone&nbsp;
related to that true history?

00:13:20.280 --> 00:13:25.440
Plus, in Japanese culture, nine is sometimes&nbsp;
considered an unlucky number because it contains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:25.440 --> 00:13:33.420
the character “ku” which means pain or&nbsp;
suffering. So maybe the Knights are in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:39.120
constant pain or are meant to protect&nbsp;
the gods from pain. And in the past,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:44.940
nine was also a number associated with the&nbsp;
Emperor, who was considered divine – basically&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:44.940 --> 00:13:49.800
a god – so it was considered taboo for&nbsp;
normal people to use the number nine.

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:56.820
And this brings us to Buddhism, which also has&nbsp;
strong ties to the number nine that might tell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:56.820 --> 00:14:02.820
us a bit more about the powers or personalities&nbsp;
of the 9 holy knights. For one there are the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.820 --> 00:14:08.040
9 holy qualities of the buddah: sharing,&nbsp;
ethical morality, patience, renunciation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:08.040 --> 00:14:15.360
wisdom, diligence, truthfulness, determination,&nbsp;
loving-kindness and equanimity. These could be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:15.360 --> 00:14:20.820
hints about their characters. Another branch&nbsp;
of the faith has something called the Nine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:20.820 --> 00:14:26.040
Consciousness, which are basically nine&nbsp;
states of being and awareness. The first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.040 --> 00:14:30.120
five states are essentially the five&nbsp;
senses: touch, taste, sight, smell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:34.320
and hearing. The sixth state involves your&nbsp;
brain processing these senses into meaningful&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.320 --> 00:14:39.000
information. The Seventh state involves becoming&nbsp;
aware of one’s inner thoughts. The eight state&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:39.000 --> 00:14:43.620
is sometimes called a storehouse containing&nbsp;
all of a person’s thoughts, words, feelings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.620 --> 00:14:49.920
and deeds throughout a lifetime. And this state&nbsp;
is said to persist even after death – Brook’s&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:56.220
matchup anyone? And the ninth, final state,&nbsp;
basically the Buddha state, is when someone rids&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:56.220 --> 00:15:03.840
themselves of all negative karma and one’s soul&nbsp;
can coexist peacefully with all lifeforms. Whew,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:08.460
there’s a lot to unpack here, but maybe I’ll&nbsp;
make a future video comparing the straw hats&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:12.540
to each of the nine states to see if we can&nbsp;
figure out who they match up against in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.540 --> 00:15:16.080
future battle. So make sure to subscribe to the&nbsp;
channel if you don’t want to miss that video.

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:25.500
But now after spending way too much time breaking&nbsp;
down this new group, let’s discuss everything else&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:30.060
that happened in this chapter and how it will&nbsp;
COMPLETELY CHANGE the One Piece world forever.

00:15:30.060 --> 00:15:34.980
So during the flashback to the reverie, we&nbsp;
see Cobra, the king of Alabasta, about to meet&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:34.980 --> 00:15:40.380
with the five elders. And at this point, we know&nbsp;
that Cobra was assassinated by someone, and that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:45.840
Luffy’s brother, Sabo was blamed for killing the&nbsp;
king. And before he goes into his meeting, Cobra&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:51.540
tells his guards that they should take care of his&nbsp;
daughter, Vivi. And now why would he say this? The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:51.540 --> 00:15:57.900
obvious answer is that he expects to not come out&nbsp;
of the room alive, which is exactly what happens.

00:15:57.900 --> 00:16:03.300
But let’s back up a little bit, because I think&nbsp;
the reason that Cobra went to talk to the Elders&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.300 --> 00:16:08.580
in the first place was because government&nbsp;
agents had already captured Vivi. Now why did&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.580 --> 00:16:13.860
they capture Vivi? Well, back in chapter 908,&nbsp;
we see Imu holding a picture of Vivi and then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:20.100
the Elders asking who Imu would like erased from&nbsp;
history. So basically they want Vivi taken out for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:20.100 --> 00:16:24.780
some reason. But back to Cobra, he probably knows&nbsp;
that his daughter has been taken and so he goes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:24.780 --> 00:16:29.670
to confront the Elders which of course leads to&nbsp;
his eventual death. However, that is not the end&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:29.670 --> 00:16:35.520
of all this, because later we see Sabo reacting to&nbsp;
Cobra’s death. This is presumably when the picture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:35.520 --> 00:16:40.440
to frame Sabo was taken, but apparently Sabo&nbsp;
was able to rescue Vivi at this point as well.

00:16:41.820 --> 00:16:47.040
But I’m also wondering if the Gorosei had another&nbsp;
reason for killing Cobra. I mean, he wasn’t their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:47.040 --> 00:16:52.440
original target, so unless it was an accident,&nbsp;
there has to be some other reason they killed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:58.200
him because killing him would throw the world&nbsp;
into even more chaos. But the only reason I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:03.660
can think of is that Cobra knows something&nbsp;
about the Void Century, and he threatened&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:03.660 --> 00:17:08.160
to reveal it unless the World Government freed&nbsp;
Vivi. Remember that the Alabsata kingdom is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:08.160 --> 00:17:13.440
only kingdom that chose to stay on their island&nbsp;
when the other original twenty kingdoms went up&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:13.440 --> 00:17:18.960
to live on Mary Geoise. Plus Alabasta was guarding&nbsp;
a Poneglyph, so that has to mean they were somehow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:18.960 --> 00:17:24.360
related to the Ancient Kingdom. So it makes&nbsp;
sense to me that Cobra would have some other&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:24.360 --> 00:17:28.560
secret information that the Elders would want&nbsp;
to keep quiet. And I don’t know about you all,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:31.860
but I am literally as excited as Gojo&nbsp;
[show Manu’s cat] with a new box as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:35.760
we get closer to finally learning&nbsp;
the secrets of the Void Century.

00:17:35.760 --> 00:17:40.500
And this is just another example of the corruption&nbsp;
in the World Government, which is the exact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:43.860
reason why the Revolutionary Army&nbsp;
has made it their mission to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:43.860 --> 00:17:48.900
down the celestial dragons. And they are&nbsp;
finally moving forward with their plans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:52.380
because in this chapter we learn that&nbsp;
they declared war by burning the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:57.660
government’s flag at Mary Geoise,&nbsp;
just like Luffy did at Enies Lobby.

00:17:59.820 --> 00:18:05.400
But unlike my boy Kakashi, these guys are&nbsp;
definitely not sneaky, because there was also&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:05.400 --> 00:18:11.160
a massive battle between the strongest fighters of&nbsp;
the Revolutionary Army and two marine admirals. We&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:11.160 --> 00:18:15.720
already knew the flame powers of Sabo, the gravity&nbsp;
powers of Fujitora, and the Forest abilities of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:15.720 --> 00:18:21.060
Greenbull, but this chapter revealed more about&nbsp;
one of the most mysterious fruits in the entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:21.060 --> 00:18:27.480
story. This guy is Karasu, who can turn into&nbsp;
a flock of crows. And he uses these crows like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:27.480 --> 00:18:32.520
bullets, as he shoots them at Fujitora. We also&nbsp;
got an official name for his fruit, the Susu&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:32.520 --> 00:18:38.520
Susu no mi, or the Soot fruit. So are these even&nbsp;
crows at all, or are crows just Karasu’s vibe?

00:18:40.320 --> 00:18:44.520
The giant okama Morley also shows some&nbsp;
impressive fighting ability when he damaged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:48.300
Greenbull with his trident. At this point&nbsp;
the revolutionaries are looking pretty good,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:48.300 --> 00:18:52.800
but everyone is really tough until the&nbsp;
gravity man whips out his ultimate attack,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:55.980
which unfortunately we&nbsp;
didn’t get to see the end of.

00:18:55.980 --> 00:19:00.600
And while this fight didn’t result in any major&nbsp;
casualties, the whole situation just continues&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:00.600 --> 00:19:05.640
to pour gas onto the dumpster fire that is the&nbsp;
world government. Because for the first time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:05.640 --> 00:19:10.140
the World Government truly appears to be losing&nbsp;
their grip on the world. Kingdoms are rebelling,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:10.140 --> 00:19:14.280
pirates and revolutionaries are declaring war.&nbsp;
They are even going to lose their scientific&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:14.280 --> 00:19:19.740
genius Dr. Vegapunk. And not one but two&nbsp;
people, Vivi and this guy who I really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:23.880
hoped to never see again [Wapol] have escaped&nbsp;
with knowledge about what really happened at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:23.880 --> 00:19:27.540
the reverie [ch 1074]. And on top of all that,&nbsp;
someone is going to find the One Piece very soon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:27.540 --> 00:19:30.840
which means the World Government’s&nbsp;
secrets are going to be spilled.

00:19:30.840 --> 00:19:34.500
But of course they aren’t going to give up&nbsp;
without a fight. And as with any evil world power,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:34.500 --> 00:19:39.480
they will surely become desperate to keep their&nbsp;
secrets and power. Who knows, maybe they will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:39.480 --> 00:19:43.800
finally unleash their ruthless fleet admiral&nbsp;
to burn the pirate world to the ground. So&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:43.800 --> 00:19:48.420
if you’re an innocent person living in a world&nbsp;
government kingdom, I would seriously consider&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:48.420 --> 00:19:53.460
finding a deserted island and hiding until this&nbsp;
epic war is over. Especially because Blackbeard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:53.460 --> 00:20:01.063
is closer than ever to finding the One Piece, and&nbsp;
he may have just confirmed that he has the most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:20:01.063 --> 00:20:06.240
broken abilities in the story. And if you want to&nbsp;
find out why, you can watch this video right here.

00:20:06.240 --> 00:20:07.860
Shanks for watching.

